      "comment": "DOLLARS (3) has the strongest winning case after putting four lengths on a small Mt Isa Quality field despite being an outside chance in betting and racing wide. He is proven around 1600m, with three wins and two placings from six attempts, and that makes him the one they have to beat. DARK HARMONY (8) is the clear danger, having started odds-on and won by six and a half lengths in a BM60 at Mt Isa, though his lack of a win from eleven runs at this distance means he may be more of a place prospect. DEFERENTIAL (7) brings honest fourths from Longreach and Birdsville, gets significant weight relief from 62kg to 56kg and had excuses wide last time. In the mix. SPANISH BLAZE (6) will be fitter again third-up so can show more.",
